# Python tests

Follow [.cursor/skills/python-tests/SKILL.md](../skills/python-tests/SKILL.md) for full conventions.

- Assert real Home Assistant behavior; no empty or tautological tests.
- Use `pytest-homeassistant-custom-component` helpers (`MockConfigEntry`, etc.).
- Keep `enable_custom_integrations` enabled via the shared autouse fixture.
- Prefer async tests that set up a config entry and assert entity/state outcomes.
- Patch network I/O at boundaries when device communication is added; do not hit real ecoNET hardware in unit tests.
